      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To convert the given point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we need to use the following transformation equations:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(\\rho = 3\\), \\(\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\), and \\(\\phi = 0\\), we simply need to substitute these values into the equations.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\cos \\phi\\):\n\\[\n\\cos \\phi = \\cos 0 = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(\\sin \\phi\\):\n\\[\n\\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, let's compute \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, compute \\(y\\):\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, compute \\(z\\):\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the rectangular coordinates are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
